stream
From: Dana Whitfield <dana.whitfield@hangs-cs.example>
To: Tax preparation <tax@finance-demo.example>
Subject: HANGS Construction Services FY2027 estimated tax, December payment
Date: Thu, 05 Nov 2026 16:10:00 -0800
Message-ID: <HCS-FY2027-ES@hangs-cs.example>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="=_HCS_FY2027_ES_request"

--=_HCS_FY2027_ES_request
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi,

The December 15 estimate is next and I want to get it right. On October 15 we=
 paid $1,324.70 by EFTPS, which with the $1,838.00 overpayment from FY2026 ma=
kes $3,162.70, a quarter of the FY2026 tax of $12,650.79. Jordan thinks we ca=
n keep paying that each quarter, the way we did before the loss year.

July to September came in at $205,803.93 of book income, well under the board=
's budget of $572,500.00 a quarter. I revised the full-year projection; it is=
 attached with the EFTPS history. The interim figures for 3, 6 and 9 months a=
re in the folder; only the first three months are closed.

Two questions:
- How much should we pay on December 15, and are we on track for the year?
- The EFTPS confirmation for October 15 shows tax period 12/2026. I think I p=
icked the calendar year out of habit. Does that matter?

Thanks,
Dana Whitfield
Controller, HANGS Construction Services LLC

--=_HCS_FY2027_ES_request
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
Content-Disposition: attachment;
 filename="FY2027 taxable income projection.xlsx"
